<title>HUNGARY: Hungary details December 1996 CPI figures.</title>
<headline>Hungary details December 1996 CPI figures.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Central Statistical Office said on Friday energy and clothing prices in December rose more than the average 0.9 percent while durable consumer goods, alcoholic beverages and tobacco price increases remained below average.</p>
<p>CONSUMER PRICE INDEX (PCT CHANGE)</p>
<p>			  Jan-Dec '96     Dec '96	  Weight in</p>
<p>			    yr/yr    mth/mth  yr/yr     index (pct)</p>
<p> Food products	 +17.3	+0.9    +15.5	   28.4</p>
<p>Alcoholic</p>
<p>beverages/</p>
<p>  tobacco products   +26.6	+0.6    +24.2	    9.5</p>
<p> Clothing		+25.6	+1.9    +24.1	    7.5 @</p>
<p>Durable consumer</p>
<p>  goods		  +19.2	+0.6    +12.5	    7.4</p>
<p> Household energy    +32.5	+1.7    +24.7	    6.5</p>
<p> Other goods, fuels  +25.7	+0.6    +20.3	   17.3</p>
<p> Services		+26.4	+0.8    +22.2	   23.4</p>
<p> Total		   +23.6	+0.9    +19.8	  100.0</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
